f 17592186045417] [17592186496247 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496142 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496247 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80656" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496247 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496247 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/5c/5c6e4deccce395f5bdc8aadef8cd2c712804235c340ccae174f2067211a5a49c.png)\n\nConsider the region $R$ shown above. Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}, & (x,y)\\in S, \\\\ {x}^{2}+y, & (x,y)\\in T, \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496247 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3fc1b49a-d775-540a-9853-9d70731cf1c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496247 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that the domain $R$ can be represented as a union of three sub-domains, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =S\\cup T\\cup U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{S}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}({x}^{2}+y)\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}0\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}({x}^{2}+y)\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496248 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496248 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80668" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496248 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496248 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$, where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2},\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<1,\\,0<y<1, \\\\ 2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y},\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<1,\\,1<y<2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  $R$ is the domain of $f.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496248 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "426d96cd-8cff-562b-8539-4a443da3b8d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496248 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that we have $R={R}_{1}\\cup {R}_{2}$, where ${R}_{1}=(0,1)\\times (0,1)$ and ${R}_{2}=(0,1)\\times (1,2).$ So, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =(1-0){\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+({\\int }_{0}^{1}2x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}{|}_{0}^{1}+({x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{1})\\cdot ({e}^{y}{|}_{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =1+1\\cdot ({e}^{2}-{e}^{1}) \\\\  & =1+{e}^{2}-e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496250 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496250 #edb/ref 1069 "q-130021" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496250 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496250 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=2,\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=7,\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n{∬}_{C\\cup D}\\frac{1}{3}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496250 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4896f06f-886c-5ec8-9b07-a29fce8c9f73" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496250 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}5f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =\\frac{1}{3}{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(7+2) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496349 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186496370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496349 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5d158e0b-364f-57cd-9861-9ba595b098dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496349 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186382462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496356 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186496361 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496356 #edb/ref 1062 #uui